  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday through Wednesday)\nIssued at 128 PM MDT Thu Apr 16 2026\n\nMuch quieter conditions are in store for Saturday, though\ntemperatures will remain on the cooler side. Most areas will have\nhigh temperatures 5 to 15 degrees below normal. Winds will remain\nlight, though will veer around to the southeast through the late\nafternoon and evening. Weak ridging moves over the state for\nSaturday night and Sunday. Breezy southerly winds will be on tap\nfor eastern NM Sunday afternoon. Very modest Gulf moisture may \nbegin to advect into southern portions of the CWA by late Sunday, \nbut not expecting any precipitation. Moisture will continue to \nincrease Sunday night into Monday, and a few light showers may \ndevelop across southeastern areas as a weak shortwave crosses the\narea. Low confidence in the upper level pattern continues for \nTuesday and beyond, but windier conditions look to return by mid \nto late week. There remains considerable uncertainty with how and \nwhen an upper level low will track across the Intermountain West.",
